      "id": "lem-av7-finite-morphism-projective-over-projective-base",
      "interface_delta": "Original algebraically closed classical finite case retained; finite-type scheme case over any field added. Finite-to-proper and finite-over-complete conclusions proved by local algebra. Global projectivity uses actual denominator clearing, overlap killing, a finite twist, one projective-space embedding and Segre; no later library Proj/properness premise."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-normal-curve-is-nonsingular",
      "interface_delta": "The perfect-field curve claim is explicitly for integral separated finite-type scheme curves, retaining the classical cases. Generic stalk is a field; nongeneric stalks are DVRs. Purely inseparable affine curve proves that perfectness is required for smoothness."
    },
    {
      "id": "cor-normalization-resolves-singularities-of-curves",
      "interface_delta": "Statement unchanged. All-field finite affine closures localize and glue; finite-type and dimension-one hypotheses are checked before applying normal-curve and generalized global projectivity suppliers."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-av7-proper-quasi-finite-factor-is-finite",
      "interface_delta": "Original proper quasi-finite classical theorem retained; exact projective finite-fiber Chevalley consequence proved from earlier projective projection closedness after every classical base change."
    },
    {
      "id": "cor-bijective-birational-to-normal-isomorphism-under-finiteness",
      "interface_delta": "Original finite birational normal-target implication retained. Added the already harvested Milne8.57 open-immersion claim via full ZMT and the reduced irreducible finite-model closure; bijectivity gives Milne8.59 without an extra finite premise."
    },
    {
